  "Question": "\\(1000 \\times 1993 \\times 0.1993 \\times 10 =\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1.993 \\times 10^3\\)",
    "B": "\\(1993.1993\\)",
    "C": "\\((199.3)^2\\)",
    "D": "\\(1{,}993{,}001.993\\)",
    "E": "\\((1993)^2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Group \\(1000\\) and \\(10\\) with the decimal. Their product is \\(10{,}000\\), so multiplying \\(0.1993\\) by them moves its decimal point four places to the right:\n\\[1000\\cdot10\\cdot0.1993=1993.\\]\nBy the commutative and associative properties of multiplication, the original product is therefore\n\\[1993\\cdot(1000\\cdot10\\cdot0.1993)=1993\\cdot1993.\\]\nThis equals \\((1993)^2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm E\\).",
